    "id": "ACT-GRAM",
    "revision": 7,
    "title": "Express anyone, nothing and not at all",
    "subtitle": "Learn, understand, and use a Mandarin pattern.",
    "context": "Use the introduced pattern in a bounded sentence. Other wording may be valid Chinese; this task checks this pattern and these words.",
    "steps": [
      {
        "id": "EX-GRAM-G-scope-indefinite-teach",
        "kind": "teach",
        "title": "Express anyone, nothing and not at all",
        "blocks": [
          {
            "text": "Question words with 都 or 也 can express unrestricted choice or, with negation, the absence of any relevant case. They need not ask for an answer. 一点儿也不… gives an emphatic negative degree, not a small positive amount.",
            "examples": [
              {
                "text": "谁想来都可以。",
                "pinyin": "shéi xiǎng lái dōu kěyǐ 。",
                "meaning": "Anyone who wants to come may come.",
                "audio": "b6aaa0bb015bebf401af2fcea053b7bc183d252bf2eab386443dae2ca8ade762"
              },
              {
                "text": "我什么都不想吃。",
                "pinyin": "wǒ shénme dōu bù xiǎng chī 。",
                "meaning": "I do not want to eat anything.",
                "audio": "a55347f7839e641b2abc267747935e7e737ac06bb50199141e1783f1b18f8a5f"
              },
              {
                "text": "我一点儿也不累。",
                "pinyin": "wǒ yīdiǎnr yě bù lèi 。",
                "meaning": "I am not at all tired.",
                "audio": "958d10064e6d6cdbc99d4845eebdb0b8d3ae832fdde52ce42c1d2b92fcaa68ad"
              }
            ]
          },
